    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting the favorable matchup against Adrian Houser. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.03) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) anchor the lineup, providing the day\u2019s highest efficiency scores. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong park factor and a solid platoon advantage, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned to thrive against Houser\u2019s 4.78 xERA; both players are set to be the primary catalysts for our offensive output. **Curtis Mead** (62.15) and **Sam Antonacci** (62.91) also register as strong starts, with **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s elite xwOBA (0.375) providing significant upside at the top of the order against Grant Holmes.\n\nWhile we are forced to navigate a difficult matchup for **Kyle Tucker** (48.01) and **Andy Pages** (44.37) against Paul Skenes, their pedigree keeps them on the field despite the suppressed projections. The most difficult bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel** (50.89); he was the closest consideration for the lineup, but he ultimately lost out to the higher situational ceiling of **Miguel Vargas** and **Liam Hicks**, whose order-of-batting advantages and platoon splits edged out **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s more modest profile. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Curtis Mead**, **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; should any of these players move down in the order or be scratched, we will need to re-evaluate our game cap strategy. Finally, take note of the wind-out conditions at several parks today, which provide a latent boost to **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Curtis Mead**, potentially raising their floors even higher than current ATC projections suggest.",
